{:db/id 17592186087697 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186087504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fa0899-a3d2-584f-8cdd-a471f8cfd16b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "79974103-2da9-599a-b33b-abac3d32613a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4392" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- $Q$ is a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. Also, all the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nNotice that $Q$ is not an identity matrix since the diagonal entries are not all ones.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, $r_{13}=1 \\neq 0$).\n\n- $S$ is a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. Also, all the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nNotice that $S$ is not an identity matrix since the diagonal entries are not all ones.\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ and $S$ are diagonal matrices."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fa0899-a3d2-584f-8cdd-a471f8cfd16b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186087985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fa0899-a3d2-584f-8cdd-a471f8cfd16b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85640f4-78cf-530b-b7b2-0f2d749a6b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459413} {:answer/id #uuid "0ef6a791-fd28-55d2-9d90-ee0d6e5ee563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85640f4-78cf-530b-b7b2-0f2d749a6b9c" :answer/type {:db/ide